course: dictionary
lesson: 4876
title: Identical: exactly the same
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Identical means exactly the same in every way. When you meet it, look for clues that things match, such as the same size, shape or colour. «Your bags are identical!» means the two bags match in every part, so you could not tell them apart.
explain: Identical twins are two babies born together who look almost exactly alike. Read the sentence: «Identical twins share the same DNA.» DNA is the instruction code inside your body, and the clue is "share the same". To check your meaning, swap it in: "identical twins share the exact same DNA" still makes sense.
explain: Phrases help you too. «Identical to» means the same as, as in "this copy is identical to the original". «Almost identical» means very close to the same, but not quite perfect. Ask yourself: is the sentence saying exactly the same, or nearly the same?
fact: Identical means exactly the same in every way.
fact: «Identical» is an adjective: it describes a noun, such as «identical twins» or «identical bags».
fact: «Almost identical» means very close to the same, but not quite perfect.
fact: The nine-banded armadillo almost always has four identical babies.
fact: Fingerprints are ridges that help us grip. Every person's fingerprints are different, even identical twins'.
exercise: «Your bags are identical!» What does identical mean? | Very large | *Exactly the same in every way | Colourful | Bought from the same shop but different
exercise: Find and copy the word that means exactly alike: «The two shapes were identical.» | shapes | two | were | *identical
exercise: Aiden says, «The two drawings are almost identical.» What does almost identical mean? | Exactly the same, with no difference at all | Completely different | Drawn in pencil | *Very close to the same, but not quite perfect
test: «Two identical shapes have the same size and shape.» What is true? | They are coloured in | They are different sizes | They are very long | *They match exactly
test: «Fingerprints are ridges that help us grip, every person's are different, even identical twins'.» Why does the author say even identical twins? | To show the twins are younger | *To show that even identical twins have different fingerprints | To show twins always wear the same clothes | To show fingerprints are the same for everyone
exam: Which sentence uses identical correctly? | *The two cups are identical: same size, same colour | The sky was identical in the morning | Please put the identical in the bin | I ate identical for lunch
